```c
/*
 * Copy-on-write support
 *
 * When an export is exported in copy-on-write mode, writes do not go to
 * the exported ("master") file. Instead, every page that is written is
 * stored in a per-connection diff file, and reads of such pages return
 * the contents of the diff file rather than those of the master file.
 * The diff file is removed when the client disconnects, so the master
 * file is left untouched.
 *
 * Two styles are supported. If the export has the sparse_cow option set,
 * the diff file is created as a sparse file that is as large as the
 * export, and pages are stored at their corresponding offset. If not,
 * every newly-written page is appended to the end of the diff file, and
 * a mapping from export page number to position in the diff file is
 * kept in memory.
 */
```

